# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree,
# regardless of the contributor's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `lib/bin.js` is the `dsh-workbuddy-connect` bin (see
# `bin` in package.json) and tsdown grants it execute permission. With CRLF on
# disk its first line is `#!/usr/bin/env node\r`, and a Unix kernel then reads
# the interpreter as `node\r` — a binary that does not exist, so the command
# fails to exec. `npm pack` ships the working tree, so packing on a Windows
# checkout publishes a broken executable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bitmap and archive assets are binary; `text=auto` already skips them, this
# makes the intent explicit and survives a future `text=auto` regression.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.wasm binary
